Marzo is a figure of the [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/index|Gulch]] who founds a city in every cycle. It has moved and its people have moved with it, but it has always been his, and he long called it [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/New Haven|Fat Cock City]]; it goes by New Haven now. He keeps to the ziggurat in the blood lake at the city's heart, working from a nexus of power there, and the Weft call him Marzu.

He guards the corpse of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] Beast that lies on the ziggurat, and the power it gives is what he has to trade. He has turned to tending the city, and he trades that power for the food, medicine and water its people need. The Weft left him the plans for an engine that would run on it.

He can reach the warden of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]]: he strums a guitar into an amplifier and the sound carries up into the black void where the warden shows itself. He spoke once to the Nightmare Heart, and he keeps a carnival beacon.
